From 9bcab47e46493f057c139c56fa2ce1a7acaf8211 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Thompson <brandon.joseph.thompson@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 10:34:34 -0700
Subject: Patch: Add process-spawn visibility to Ryoku Shell.

Centralizes every process spawn across the shell, ryolayer, ryowalls,
hub, ryovm, and the lockscreen behind a shared Spawn wrapper
(ryoku/shared/quickshell/) that captures stdout/stderr to a log file,
deletes it on a clean exit, and fires a desktop notification with a
"View log" action on failure. The launcher's own copy additionally
tracks a live registry so search results show "(N launched)" next to
the app name and "View log(s)" appears in the Ctrl+K action panel for
anything still running or that failed.

Adapted for beta-18, which grew substantially past what this patch
was written against:
- A whole new ryolayer widget system (shell.qml, Eq.qml, MicWidget.qml,
  NotesWidget.qml) got wired into the shared Spawn wrapper too, plus
  its own Singletons/qmldir symlinks -- none of this existed when the
  original patch was authored.
- Several more hub pages needed the same treatment (KeybindsPage,
  StorePage, SettingsSheet) beyond the original's DictationPage/
  FastfetchPage/GpuPage/LockscreenPage/PerformancePage/RashinPage/
  UpdatesPage/PageHeader -- hub pages also moved under quickshell/pages/
  in beta-18's schema-driven redesign, so every page needed a fresh
  `import "../Singletons"` rather than reusing the original diff's
  context.
- Pill grew Toggles.qml (DeckControls' wifi/mic/night-light toggles,
  refactored into a shared singleton), AtollBar/DyadBar/BarModularFace
  and their popouts (AtollBatteryPopout, AtollMusicPopout, PowerAction),
  none of which existed in the original patch's target tree.
- ryovm grew Remotes.qml (SSH host management), not in the original.
- Devices.qml's backlight functions were ported through their beta-18
  names (setBacklight/reportBacklightChange from this branch's own
  0004 redesign) rather than main's panelBrightness-era names, which
  don't exist here.
- Apps.qml's terminal-vs-GUI launch split uses entry.command/
  workingDirectory/runInTerminal -- verified these exist on Quickshell's
  DesktopEntry type (checked the installed qmltypes) since this
  provider had no existing Quickshell.execDetached call for the diff to
  anchor on.

Also carries the two pre-existing bug fixes the original wiring
surfaced: activateEntry()'s window-focus script returning a spurious
failure whenever the clicked notification's sender has no matching
window (now `; true`), and the Inbox group header re-showing a
critical notification's own content a second time when it had nothing
else to preview (preview now null instead of falling back to it, with
matching null-guards in Notifs.ageLabel and Inbox.qml's text binding).
